+## Native message identity
+
+Chat's versioned `uiChatChrome` capability elects pure appearance data for existing native wrappers; the identity-only `conversation.chat.message.chrome` Factory owns the header and avatar Slots without taking a body or renderer continuation. Both Slots receive [`ChatMessageOwner`](../../packages/client/ui-chat/src/client/contract/message-chrome.ts) and ordinary Session hooks, including `useProjection`. Native keys, body outlets, controls, and visibility remain host-owned; containing frames and Turn controls are transparent. The [ui-chat reference](../../packages/client/ui-chat/README.md#native-message-decoration) defines priority, disposal, layout, and settings deployment semantics.
